From 88e3f9c22dc87df52e48a9ca0405b168407dee45 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Proofloom <fix@proofloom.local>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 19:55:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Fix 'Too many properties to enumerate': bounded Hunspell
 checking for all languages

nspell expands every affix rule for every dictionary word at parse time.
Morphologically rich language packs (Italian it_IT: 3,233 affix entries,
95k words with clitic continuation classes) explode into millions of
generated forms: the worker hangs for minutes and the browser's
dictionary object grows past V8's key-enumeration limits, surfacing as
'RangeError: Too many properties to enumerate' and killing the local
check for non-English text.

Replace the parse-time expander with a bounded reader:

- src/core/algorithms/hunspell.js (new): capped affix/dic parser plus a
  reverse-application membership checker. Handles surface forms, case
  (exact/lower/sentence, KEEPCASE), NEEDAFFIX, FORBIDDENWORD, multi-level
  continuation chains, and combineable prefix/suffix cross-products.
  Per-query work is bounded (25k ops); models are cached per pack version.
- Pack pairs beyond the caps (or with legacy encodings) fall back to
  surface-form membership, so checking keeps working for every language.
- Pack vocabulary joins the candidate indexes, so suggestions work for
  every language (deletion, phonetic, keyboard, split, and new
  extra-character deletion candidates), ranked by the weighted scorer.
- check() accepts a deadline and reports engine.lastCheck.timedOut; the
  worker wraps every check in a 30s budget and posts a degraded flag
  instead of hanging; the editor shows a notice when degraded.
- Worker errors are logged with full stack for diagnosis.

Measured with the LibreOffice Italian dictionary (95,438 entries):
before, parsing never completed (>5 min hang); after, configure is 95ms
and a 3-paragraph check runs in 24-32ms warm (~2s once for index
build), with zero false positives on correct Italian and working
suggestions for typos (gattto -> gatto).

Tests: 11 new cases in tests/hunspell.test.mjs; suite 94/94.
